    {
      "_id": "sXc3d4dCmSsEKrrJ",
      "name": "Frost Breath {@recharge 5}",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/svg/sword.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>The drake exhales an icy blast in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a DC 16 Dexterity saving throw, taking 31 ([[/damage 7d8 cold]]) on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature who fails their saving throw has their movement speed halved and can't take reactions for 1 minute. If they fail their save by 5 or more, they are also entombed in ice.\n\nWhile entombed, they have total cover and are restrained and incapacitated. At the beginning of their turn, they take 9 ([[/damage 2d8 cold]]) and can attempt a DC 16 Strength check, breaking free from the ice on a success. The ice can be attacked and destroyed (AC 10; hp equal to cold damage taken by the breath weapon; vulnerability to fire damage; immunity to cold, poison, and psychic damage).</p>",
